[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2748289192","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104553#issuecomment-2748289192","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104553","id":2748289192,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jz5Co","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T14:17:21Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T14:51:03Z","body":"I really like the idea of extending `constexpr` use in general!\r\n\r\nBut I think I'd have to be sold on the benefits for every type individually, because adding `constexpr` to everything adds a lot of boilerplate. `RID` seems like something that's rarely known at compile time, because it will be generated at runtime. That would limit its use as a `constexpr` object.\r\n\r\nI'm also not sold on all `static_assert` compile time testing, but that's probably a different discussion to be had.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2748289192/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2748695177","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104553#issuecomment-2748695177","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104553","id":2748695177,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j1cKJ","user":{"login":"YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333","html_url":"https://github.com/YYF233333","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T16:19:19Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T16:19:19Z","body":"> But I think I'd have to be sold on the benefits for every type individually, because adding `constexpr` to everything adds a lot of boilerplate. `RID` seems like something that's rarely known at compile time, because it will be generated at runtime. That would limit its use as a `constexpr` object.\r\n\r\nBoilerplate is an issue, but I feel that in order to support tests outside of `core` using `static_assert` (though I'm not sure how many actually exist), introducing a large number of `constexpr` in `core` is inevitable. This is because, for a type to be usable at compile-time, all of its member functions must be `constexpr`. \r\n\r\nSo the real question is to what extent we want to migrate tests to compile-time. E.g. this PR adds `constexpr` to `RID` specifically to allow `static_assert` in `test_rid`.\r\n\r\nP.S. The binary size improvement comes from adding `constexpr` to the constructor, though I'm not entirely sure about the mechanism behind it.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2748695177/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2748708676","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104553#issuecomment-2748708676","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104553","id":2748708676,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j1fdE","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T16:24:02Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T16:24:30Z","body":"> So the real question is to what extent we want to migrate tests to compile-time. E.g. this PR adds constexpr to RID specifically to allow static_assert in test_rid.\r\n\r\nAgreed. I think this idea would be worth making into a proper GIP to be assessed.\r\n\r\n> P.S. The binary size improvement comes from adding constexpr to the constructor, though I'm not entirely sure about the mechanism behind it.\r\n\r\nThat's interesting, I'd think `_ALWAYS_INLINE_` sufficiently takes care of that. Hard to say for sure what's happening, but 4kb (while a respectable improvement) is probably not worth digging too deeply into.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2748708676/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2750169550","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104553#issuecomment-2750169550","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104553","id":2750169550,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j7EHO","user":{"login":"YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333","html_url":"https://github.com/YYF233333","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-25T05:56:56Z","updated_at":"2025-03-25T05:56:56Z","body":"> On the note of readability though, maybe we should consider a macro like `CONSTEXPR_INLINE` that's just `_ALWAYS_INLINE_ constexpr`? Seems like a good chunk of the `constexpr` additions still benefit from forced inlines\r\n\r\nAdd `_ALWAYS/FORCE_CONSTEXPR_INLINE_`, not very satisified with the name, maybe `COMPTIME` will show our purpose better. There are other candidates with `_FORCE_INLINE_` attribute so I kept `ALWAYS/FORCE` prefix for now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2750169550/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]